@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] updater-verifies-before-install
The updater installs only an APK whose SHA-256 matches `latest.json` and whose
`versionCode` is higher than the installed one; a mismatch is an error and nothing is
installed. Installation goes through Android's own installer and its approval.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] updater-asks-only-its-server
Updates come only from the configured server's `/download/latest.json` (Pully Staging:
`/download/staging/latest.json`, android `android-staging-channel`) and the APK it names,
with the same Access headers as every other request. No third-party update
service or library is in the path.
The manifest MUST name a binary APK URL rather than the `/download` HTML page.
Source: Tavi's 22 Oct 2026 download-page and removed direct-APK decision.
Anonymous Explore MUST NOT start configured private-server update checks, downloads or
installation from an old notification. A late check MUST NOT change the guest's state.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 signed-out public browsing and separate entry-authority plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] updater-remembers-the-offer
The phone remembers the last offer, so the update screen is there before the server
answers again, and the offer goes once the server has nothing newer (rule 104).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] updater-notifies-once
A new version is told in a notification while the app is closed, once per version
(rule 104).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] updater-update-pulls-command
Update Pully in Commands asks the server at once and starts the update, or says this is
the newest version (rule 104).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] updater-installation-recovers
An update MUST persist its own installer session and target version before handing bytes
to Android. Only callbacks for that session MAY change its result. Confirmation MUST be
opened by the resumed activity and remain available when the reader returns. Interrupted
or expired installs MUST offer retry, and only the installed package version MAY settle
success. Source: Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, updates stuck at installing or downloading; rule 63.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] past-versions-install-beside
A past version installs only from the configured server's `/download/past/`, only when
its SHA-256 matches `index.json`, and only as its own `com.octaviantocan.pulls.v*`
package: the installer is told the package name, so a past build can never replace
this app. Its versionCode is offset so no update is ever offered to it.
The canonical namespace follows Tavi's 22 Oct 2026 download-page decision; existing
read-only history aliases MAY remain for older installed clients.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] past-versions-get-the-server-at-launch
A past version gets the server address and Access token only in the explicit intent
that opens it, and only when its package is signed with this app's key; nothing else
exposes them to other apps. Its activity is behind a signature permission, so no other
app can open it and point it at another server.
